- [[ Marinus of Tyre ]], [[ Hellenic | hellenistic-period ]][[ geographer ]], [[ cartographer ]] and [[ mathematician ]] whose works greatly influenced [[ Ptolemy | claudius-ptolemy ]]'s famous //[[ Geography | geography-ptolemy ]]// as acknowledged by Ptolemy
- [[ Ulpian ]] (early 3rd century AD), Famous Roman jurist who taught at the renowned [[ Law school | law-school-of-berytus ]] at [[ Beirut ]]
- Meropius of Tyre (Μερόπιος), a philosopher, traveled together with two of his relatives, Frumentius (Φρουμέντιος) and Edesius (Εδέσιος) to ancient India.[[ ^147 ]][[ ^148 ]]
- [[ Saint Christina of Tyre | christina-of-bolsena ]] (3rd century AD) Martyr[[ ^149 ]]
